comments.body:
@Sirraide I've moved the fix to `Sema::AddKnownFunctionAttributes()` and added a release note.

The crash is fixed, but the outer `a(...)` call still emits the nonliteral-format warning after the undeclared-function and integer-to-pointer conversion errors.

I experimented locally with suppressing this cascading diagnostic in `CheckFormatArguments()`:

``` cc
const Expr *FormatExpr = Args[format_idx]->IgnoreParens();
const auto *FormatCast = dyn_cast<ImplicitCastExpr>(FormatExpr);
if (FormatExpr->containsErrors() ||
    (FormatCast && FormatCast->getCastKind() == CK_IntegralToPointer))
  return false;
```

I checked integer-to-pointer conversions separately because such a conversion can produce an implicit cast without marking the expression as containing errors.

However, this approach seems to introduce another issue: when `-Wint-conversion` is disabled or downgraded to a warning, this logic still suppresses the format warning, even though there is no corresponding conversion error. For that reason, I have left this change out of the updated patch for now.

I'm not quite sure how best to handle this cascading diagnostic. What do you think would be a good direction to explore?

