Related PR: #228863
Original Issue: #225037

While working on #225037, where using an enum as the element type of `ext_vector_type` triggers an assertion failure, we added regression tests covering template instantiation in PR #228863 and discovered an additional diagnostic location issue. This issue also reproduces without the changes from PR #228863, using a struct as the element type.

For the test case below, instantiating `Vector<S>` correctly produces an error about the invalid element type. However, the primary error diagnostic does not include a filename, line number, or column number, nor does it display the corresponding source line. In contrast, the note pointing to the template instantiation has a valid source location.

Reproducer (https://godbolt.org/z/rToTWfrxj):

``` cc
struct S {};

template <typename T> struct Vector {
  typedef T type __attribute__((ext_vector_type(4)));
};

Vector<S> struct_vector;
```

Actual output:

``` txt
error: invalid vector element type 'S'
<source>:7:11: note: in instantiation of template class 'Vector<S>' requested here
    7 | Vector<S> struct_vector;
      |           ^
1 error generated.
```

Expected behavior:

The primary error diagnostic should include a valid source location pointing to the relevant `ext_vector_type` attribute in the template, while preserving the existing template instantiation note.

Related discussion: https://github.com/llvm/llvm-project/pull/228863#discussion_r4188767251

